<!--
  sitemap.xml — youngarchitects.in

  ONE URL, ON PURPOSE. A sitemap is a list of pages you are asking to have
  indexed, so it must only ever contain indexable URLs. Every other page this
  site exports is a Coming Soon placeholder that ships
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow"> from
  src/app/(site)/[...slug]/page.jsx. Listing those here would contradict the
  page itself, and Search Console reports it as "Submitted URL marked
  noindex" — a warning against the whole sitemap, not just the offending row.

  ADDING A PAGE. When a placeholder is replaced by a real page, that page stops
  emitting the noindex tag — add its URL here at the same time. Keep the
  trailing slash: next.config.mjs sets trailingSlash: true, so /our-services/seo/
  is the canonical form and /our-services/seo would be a redirect.

  To check what is currently indexable, build and grep the export:
    npx next build
    grep -rLi "noindex" out --include=index.html

  changefreq and priority are omitted deliberately. Google has confirmed it
  ignores both, and unread hints are just another thing to keep in step.
-->
